# how the embed is cached. the two tiers are not interchangeable, and the short one is the
# load-bearing half.
#
# `<script src="https://…/embed.js" async>` is pasted into sites this project cannot reach and is
# never edited again, so /embed.js is the only request an already-pasted snippet repeats. cache it
# long and an upgrade arrives nowhere: there is no version to bump on the org's page and nobody to
# ask. it is re-read every few minutes instead, and each read already carries the path of the
# runtime it should load. Cloudflare attaches an ETag to a static asset by default, so a re-read
# that finds nothing new costs a 304 rather than the file.
#
# the runtime under /embed is named by the hash of its own contents, so a new build is a new URL
# and that tier is never revalidated.
#
# scripts/embed-headers.spec.ts holds both tiers to this — including against a later rule
# that covers /embed.js without naming it, since a request inherits the headers of every rule
# whose pattern matches.
#
# this file is in static/ because that is the public directory (../vite.config.ts): vite copies it
# whole into build/client/, which is the assets directory the built worker uploads, and cloudflare
# reads a `_headers` file at the root of the assets it is serving.

/embed.js
	Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate
	X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff

/embed/*
	Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
	X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
